Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- extract-exercises.py doesn't detect OpenStax's bold-mathvariant mstyle
  wrapping vector quantities (r, i, j, k, T, N, B), so it emitted plain
  \text{r}, \text{i}, etc. instead of \mathbf{...} for the position,
  tangent, normal, and binormal vectors throughout this file (same
  systemic gap already patched for vol3-3-1 and vol3-3-2). Converted every
  such occurrence to \mathbf{...}.
- Several bare prose variables and inequalities were left as plain text
  instead of math mode: "y axis"/"x-axis" (inconsistently hyphenated) and
  bare coordinate values in the figure descriptions for items 5, 18, and
  28 (e.g. "x = 0.3", "y=20", "-4 and 4"); "Write r as a parameter of s."
  in item 26; the repeated "arc-length parameter s" in items 27-28; the
  plane curve "C" and "as t increases" in the paragraph/items introducing
  the last group; "about the y-axis" and "as a function of x" in the cup
  problem; and "the parameter t" / "the x-coordinate" in items 30 and 30
  (curvature-of-1/x and the ellipse-curvature item). Wrapped each in math
  mode ($x$-axis, $y$-axis, $y=20$, $-4$, $4$, $\mathbf{r}$, $s$, $C$,
  $t$, $x$) to match the surrounding notation.

